{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only observed data variable scored by a sampling statement is the top-level variable `y`, and it is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement after all parameter priors have been declared. The other data variables (`J`, `N`, and `county`) are context inputs used as sizes/indices and are not protected.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> J;
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector[J] eta;
  real mu;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_eta;
  real<lower=0, upper=100> sigma_y;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[N] y_hat;

  for (i in 1 : N) {
    y_hat[i] = 0.1 * mu + eta[county[i]];
  }
}
model {
  sigma_eta ~ uniform(0, 100);
  sigma_y ~ uniform(0, 100);
  mu ~ normal(0, 1);
  eta ~ normal(0, sigma_eta);
  y ~ normal(y_hat, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J": 2, "N": 3, "county": [1, 1, 1], "y": [3.0, 3.0, 3.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
